details:
(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM JANMAN) for the development of Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs);
(b) the key interventions in health, education, housing, connectivity and livelihood support provided to PVTG habitations; and
(c) the number of beneficiaries covered and infrastructure projects completed since the launch of the PM JANMAN scheme?

(a) whether preparatory activities for Census 2027, including House Listing and Housing Census, have commenced across all States and Union Territories;
(b) the State-wise status of digital infrastructure and self-enumeration facilities for Census, 2027;
(c) whether training programmes have been conducted for census functionaries and supervisors;
(d) whether any funds have been released to States and Union Territories for census-related activities; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) extent of participation under National Youth Parliament Scheme (NYPS) 2.0 since its launch, including number of institutions registered, sittings conducted under each mode and participants enrolled through the portal;
(b) current status of implementation of the Consultative Committee Management System (CCMS), including number of Ministries and Consultative Committees onboarded thereon;
(c) steps taken to promote wider participation in the NYPS particularly among rural areas, smaller educational institutions and socially disadvantaged groups; 
(d) whether Government proposes to further strengthen the NYPS and CCMS through measures such as curriculum integration, capacity building and digital upgradation; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the key initiatives undertaken by the Ministry for the implementation of the SARAL Steel Import Monitoring System (SARAL SIMS);
(b) the details of the integration of the simplified registration mechanism with the existing Steel Import Monitoring System (SIMS) to facilitate ease of compliance for importers;
(c) the categories of importers and steel products covered under SARAL SIMS;
(d) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of the impact of SARAL SIMS on trade facilitation and Ease of Doing Business; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of countries with which India has signed Memoranda of Understanding or cooperation agreements for Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI), along with the key areas of cooperation;
(b) the details of all such agreements;
(c) the progress made in implementation of these agreements, including deployment of India's digital public goods and capacity-building initiatives in partner countries;
(d) the institutional framework adopted for coordinating DPI partnerships with partner countries and the concerned Ministries and agencies; and
(e) the roadmap for expanding India's international cooperation on Digital Public Infrastructure, particularly with the countries of Global South during the next three years?

(a) the progress achieved in developing domestic mineral processing, beneficiation and recycling capacity for key minerals, including critical and strategic minerals as of May, 2026;
(b) the details of new processing units, recycling facilities and value-addition infrastructure established under Government initiatives;
(c) whether integration of mineral beneficiation with downstream industries such as electronics, EVs and renewable energy has been undertaken;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the impact achieved in terms of import substitution, value addition and supply chain resilience?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed the progress of implementation of White Revolution 2.0 and if so, the outcome thereof;
(b) the State-wise progress in establishment of new dairy cooperative societies and strengthening of existing societies under the initiative;
(c) whether the Ministry has taken steps to enhance milk procurement and dairy infrastructure under the initiative;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) whether any financial assistance has been released to States and implementing agencies for the initiative; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the objectives and key features of BharatTradeNet, particularly about digitisation and integration of India's international trade ecosystem;
(b) the extent of integration of the platform with Customs, logistics providers, banks and other trade facilitation agencies;
(c) the proposed sectoral and geographical coverage of the platform, along with the phased implementation roadmap; and
(d) the planned investment, including the contribution of the Centre and partner agencies, for implementation of BharatTradeNet?

(a) whether the Ministry has released the draft Telecommunications (Television, Radio and Associated Services) Rules, 2026 to consolidate multiple existing broadcasting guidelines into a single regulatory framework under the Telecommunications Act, 2023;
(b) if so, the key features proposed in these draft rules;
(c) whether timelines have been set for finalisation and implementation of the Rules; and 
(d) the measures proposed to support industry transition to the new regulatory framework?

(a) the objectives and salient provisions of the Scheme to Promote Manufacturing of Electric Passenger Cars in India (SPMEPCI), particularly in the context of attracting investment and promoting domestic manufacturing;
(b) whether the scheme has a provision for the localization of manufacturing and transfer of technology, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of the proposed investment, manufacturing capacity, and employment generation under the scheme; and
(d) the framework for the implementation of the scheme, including the role of the Central Government and the participating manufacturers?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana in creating modern food processing infrastructure and value addition facilities in all States including Maharashtra;
(b) the number of projects sanctioned, completed, and the employment generated through the scheme district-wise including Maharashtra;
(c) the steps taken to reduce post-harvest losses, promote farmer producer organisations, and enhance farmer income especially in the Khandesh and Marthwada rigion of Maharashtra; and
(d) the overall impact on food processing capacity, exports and growth of the sector?

(a) the progress made under the IndiaAI Mission till May 2026, including the initiatives launched pursuant to the India Artificial Intelligence (AI) Governance Guidelines;
(b) the status of development of indigenous AI foundation models, common compute infrastructure and AI datasets under the Mission;
(c) the measures taken to promote the adoption and development of artificial intelligence by Startups, Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) and academic institutions in the country including Uttar Pradesh; and
(d) the safeguards put in place to ensure responsible, transparent and secure deployment of AI technologies?

(a) whether the National Level Policy Implementation and Monitoring Committee has reviewed the implementation of the National Cooperation Policy, 2025;
(b) if so, the decisions taken thereon;
(c) whether the Ministry has finalised a monitoring framework and implementation roadmap under the Policy;
(d) the State-wise status of verification and updation of cooperative societies on the National Cooperative Database;
(e) whether the National Cooperative Database has been integrated with the implementation of the National Cooperation Policy; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made under the Deendayal Divyangjan Rehabilitation Scheme (DDRS) during the last three years, including the institutions and beneficiaries covered;
(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised under the scheme, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has taken steps to strengthen awareness and participation of voluntary organisations under the scheme, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to improve access to rehabilitation, early intervention and community-based support services for Persons with Disabilities (PwD)?
bs

(a) whether Government has taken steps to expand the skill development ecosystem in the country during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the progress of Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY);
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether PMKVY 4.0 has introduced any measure for improving quality and transparency in skill training; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the progress of construction of National High-Speed Corridors and Greenfield Expressways during 2026 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) State-wise status of ongoing and completed National High-Speed Corridor and Expressway projects, including the length awarded, under construction and completed so far;
(c) whether any measures have been taken to expedite completion of delayed highway and expressway projects through revised implementation mechanisms or contractual reforms; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the objectives and key components of the initiative for integrated development of 500 reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars announced in the Union Budget 2026–27;
(b) whether reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars have been identified for implementation of the initiative, if so, the criteria adopted therefor;
(c) the proposed coverage of Fish Farmer Producer Organisations (Fish FPOs), women-led groups and fisheries cooperatives under the initiative; and
(d) the planned investment, including the contribution of the Centre and the States, for implementation of the initiative?

(a) the details of the allocation of capital expenditure during the period 2021-2026;
(b) the details of the ‘Effective Capital Expenditure’ including Grants-in-Aid for the creation of capital assets for the financial years 2021-26;
(c) the details of the trends of capital expenditure as a percentage of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) during the said periods and its impact on infrastructure development; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to further accelerate effective capital expenditure in the coming years?

(a) the outcomes of the expansion of the Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana (PMGKAY) since January 2025; 
(b) whether the Government has conducted any assessment or evaluation of the effectiveness or impact of the scheme in providing support to vulnerable sections during economic challenges; 
(c) if so, the details thereof; and 
(d) the future action plan regarding this scheme, including proposed amendments, technical improvements, or convergence with other welfare schemes, and the details thereof?

(a) the existing policy for deciding and printing Maximum Retail Price (MRP) on packaged goods;
(b) whether there is any upper limit for printing of MRP;
(c) why there is no statutory provisions under The Legal Metrology Act providing for ceiling limit on MRP, given that printing of MRP is a statutory requirement;
(d) whether Government is considering requests of Akhil Bhartiya Grahak Panchayat to frame any rules or regulations for printing of MRP on packaged goods; and
(e) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by Government thereon?

(a) whether Government has considered making it mandatory to print the actual manufacturing cost of every packaged commodity, in addition to the Maximum Retail Price (MRP), to enhance transparency and protect consumer interests;
(b) whether Government proposes to introduce or strengthen a statutory or regulatory mechanism for the fixation of MRP of packaged commodities so as to prevent excessive mark-ups and ensure fair pricing for consumers;
(c) if so, the details thereof and the proposed timeline for implementation; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the total production of Urea in the country during the period after 2014 as compared to the decade prior to 2014, year-wise;
(b) whether the country has moved significantly closer to self-sufficiency in urea production after 2014;
(c) the steps taken by Government since 2014 to augment indigenous production capacity of Urea; and
(d) the impact of these measures on reducing import dependence as compared to the pre- 2014 period?

(a) the present status of implementation of MSME Cluster Development Programme, including number of Common Facility Centres (CFCs) established and operational as of May 2026, State and district-wise including the State of Assam;
(b) the details of infrastructure created under cluster development projects, including testing labs, training centres and shared production facilities;
(c) whether integration of MSME clusters with supply chains, vendor networks and export-oriented production systems has been undertaken;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the impact achieved on value addition, employment generation and competitiveness of MSME clusters?

(a) the key features of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) 2.0 and the major changes that have been made in it as compared to the previous phase of the Mission;
(b) the implementation framework and funding pattern under the Mission;
(c) the reforms proposed to strengthen source sustainability, operation and maintenance of rural water supply systems and community participation;
(d) the State-wise funds allocated and released under JJM 2.0 during the year 2026-27; and
(e) the timeline and targets for achieving universal and sustainable rural household tap water supply under the Mission?

(a) the status of implementation of the Urban Challenge Fund (UCF), including the framework for project selection, funding pattern and progress achieved during Financial Year 2025-26;
(b) whether guidelines have been issued for selection of cities and projects under the UCF;
(c) the sectors proposed to be covered, including redevelopment of cities, water and sanitation infrastructure and urban mobility;
(d) the planned financial outlay, including the contribution of the Centre, States and other stakeholders; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to promote coal gasification and other cleaner coal technologies during 2026 including the State of Bihar;
(b) the number of coal gasification projects approved or under implementation, and their current status;
(c) whether any financial incentives or viability gap funding mechanisms have been introduced to support such projects, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the expected improvement in coal utilisation efficiency and reduction in emissions and enhancing domestic energy security through these technologies?

(a) the progress of Mission Karmayogi with iGOT, including National Virtual Centre for Experiential Training (NCVET) recognition of Karmayogi Bharat SPV;
(b) the progress achieved in capacity-building initiatives under Mission Karmayogi, including training on new criminal laws, the launch of District Karmayogi and the preparation of State-level implementation plans;
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed impact on civil services competency and proposes Phase II expansion; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of increasing renewable energy penetration on grid stability, and;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the steps taken to expand transmission infrastructure for renewable energy evacuation;
(d) the number of renewable energy projects facing delays due to grid connectivity constraints;
(e) whether energy storage systems are being integrated with renewable energy projects;
(f) if so, the extent of integration thereof;
(g) whether Government is implementing large-scale renewable energy corridors under the Green Energy Corridor initiative; and
(h) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the manner in which the inclusion of ‘ergonomic berths’ and advanced noise-reduction technology has improved the overnight travel experience of passengers;
(b) the specific progress made towards the target of launching 30 new sleeper rakes by December 2026;
(c) whether the Ministry has successfully completed the testing of the 24-coach Vande Bharat Sleeper prototype at the Integral Coach Factory (ICF), Chennai;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the extent of reduction in travel time on the Howrah–Guwahati corridor as compared to conventional superfast express trains?

(a) the number of public EV charging stations approved and made operational under the Faster Adoption and Manufacturing of Hybrid and Electric Vehicles (FAME-II) scheme, including Mahrashtra and Uttar Pradesh;
(b) whether the charging stations are evenly distributed across various districts of the States;
(c) if so, the details of such distribution, district-wise;
(d) whether the utilization rate of the installed EV chargers in the States have been assessed;
(e) if so, the details of the results of such assessment;
(f) whether interoperability standards are being implemented in the charging network; and
(g) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the cumulative capacity committed under the Advanced Chemistry Cell (ACC) PLI scheme in GWh;
(b) the status of land acquisition and plant commissioning for approved firms;
(c) whether domestic cell manufacturing has reduced import dependency for EV batteries;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) whether technology transfer arrangements have been finalised with global partners; and
(f) if so, the details of such arrangements?

(a) the number of Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)-recognised startups as on date;
(b) whether tax and compliance relaxations have improved startup survival rates;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether funding access outside Tier-1 cities has improved;
(e) if so, the details thereof;
(f) whether sectoral diversification beyond fintech and e-commerce is being encouraged; and
(g) if so, the measures taken in that regard?

(a) the total number and value of projects sanctioned under the Agriculture Infrastructure Fund (AIF);
(b) the sector-wise and region-wise distribution of warehousing, cold storage, primary processing, particularly in Rajasthan;
(c) whether disbursement of sanctioned loans is proceeding as per schedule, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measurable outcomes shown by post-harvest loss indicators?

(a) whether the merger of Swadhar Greh and Ujjawala under Mission Shakti into Shakti Sadan has improved service delivery and rehabilitation outcomes for women in distress;
(b) whether the Ministry has conducted any assessment of the adequacy of existing functional Shakti Sadans in meeting the demand across States/UTs;
(c) whether Government maintains any data on the number of women rehabilitated and successfully reintegrated under the scheme;
(d) if so, details and status thereof; and
(e) whether any monitoring mechanism is in place to ensure that vocational training and social security linkages are effectively implemented for residents?

(a) whether the Ministry has assessed the progress made under the PM-AJAY across its three components;
(b) if so, details of the State-wise allocation and utilisation of funds under the scheme;
(c) the total number of SC-dominated villages developed as Adarsh Gram;
(d) whether the Ministry has assessed poverty reduction in SC communities, improvement in school enrolment and livelihood gains in aspirational districts and SC-dominated blocks;
(e) if so, the details thereof; and
(f) the roadmap to expand coverage with enhanced grants-in-aid for comprehensive livelihood projects and infrastructure development?

(a) the details of the number of PPP projects operating at major ports;
(b) the details of total private investment mobilized in port infrastructure during the last five years;
(c) whether any PPP projects have faced financial difficulties or contract renegotiation;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps taken to standardize concession agreements for port PPP projects?

(a) the current maternal mortality ratio and infant mortality rates in the country;
(b) whether Government has identified districts with high maternal mortality rates;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) the steps taken to strengthen institutional delivery services under the Ministry's flagship schemes;
(e) whether additional incentives are being provided to encourage more check-ups for antenatal care; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has integrated AYUSH facilities with the national digital health ecosystem under Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of AYUSH practitioners registered on digital health platforms and issuing digital health records;
(c) whether telemedicine services based on AYUSH systems have been operationalised in rural and remote areas, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry proposes to develop AI-based tools for AYUSH diagnosis, drug standardisation or treatment protocols, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps taken to create a national digital repository of classical AYUSH formulations and therapies?
