(a) the key indicators currently included in the National Indicator Framework (NIF) for monitoring India’s progress towards Sustainable Development Goals;
(b) the frequency by which Government update the State Indicator Framework (SIF) to reflect the unique development priorities of different States;
(c) whether Government has successfully integrated data from the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) into the annual SDG progress reports;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) when was the last SDG National Indicator Framework Progress Report released and the major highlights regarding poverty alleviation and gender equality; and
(f) details of the collaboration between MoSPI and international agencies to ensure India’s SDG reporting remains globally comparable and transparent?

(a) the current number of ongoing infrastructure projects valued at ?150 crore and above that are being monitored by Government;
(b) the manner in which introduction of the Project Assessment, Infrastructure Monitoring and Analytics for Nation-Building (PAIMANA) web-portal improved the real-time tracking of delays and cost overruns in central sector projects;
(c) whether Government provides specific recommendations to administrative Ministries when a project exceeds its original sanctioned cost by more than 20 per cent;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) details of the mechanism used to coordinate with the Project Monitoring Group (PMG) to resolve inter-ministerial bottlenecks for delayed projects?

(a) specific financial incentives, such as interest subvention rates, provided to micro and small enterprises under the Assistance in Deploying Energy Efficient Technologies in Industries and Establishments (ADEETIE) scheme launched in July 2025;
(b) the number of industrial sectors and clusters currently covered under the ADEETIE scheme for energy efficiency handholding;
(c) whether all 36 States including Bihar and Union Territories have successfully transitioned to issuing electricity bills in regional languages with simplified formats;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) details of methodology and industry sectors currently notified under Carbon Credit Trading Scheme launched in 2023?

(a) whether Government has successfully commenced the construction of the Phase II Strategic Petroleum Reserves in Chandikhole (Odisha) and Padur (Karnataka);
(b) the manner in which the newly introduced Commercial-cum-Strategic storage model has successfully attracted international oil majors to store crude oil in Indian caverns;
(c) the specific success Indian Strategic Petroleum Reserves Limited (ISPRL) has recorded in maintaining the national 74-day supply cushion during the global oil price volatility; and
(d) the manner in which the increased allocation of ?200 crore for Mission Anveshan in the 2026-27 Budget has helped the ONGC Videsh Limited (OVL) in securing new overseas energy assets in the Andaman and Nicobar basins?

(a) the manner in which the price ceiling of $6.75/MMBTU for gas from nomination fields of Oil and Natural Gas Corporation (ONGC) and Oil India Limited (OIL) shielded consumers from volatility in the Gas Index of India;
(b) the positive outcomes achieved in sustaining domestic exploration investment by maintaining the ceiling of $9.72/MMBTU for gas produced from difficult fields until March, 2031;
(c) the progress made towards increasing the share of natural gas in the primary energy mix to 15 per cent target by 2030 under the roadmap for a gas-based economy; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of Bharat Small Reactors (BSRs) optimised for industrial captive power and decarbonisation near steel/aluminium plants;
(b) the details of land required for such reactors and sites identified for their deployment;
(c) whether the Department has assessed commercial viability of such reactors and proposes Bharat Small Reactor Policy; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) how the Ministry proposes to ensure safe and regulated migration pathways under the India–EU co-operation framework;
(b) whether there are any plans to align skill development initiatives in the North Eastern Region (NER) with labour market requirements of European countries;
(c) the measures taken to prevent irregular migration while promoting lawful mobility channels;
(d) whether student outreach initiatives are being institutionalised to expand awareness about higher education and professional opportunities in Europe; and
(e) if so, what specific opportunities are available for students from NER?

(a) the progress achieved under the MISHTI scheme for mangrove restoration across States and Union Territories especially in Maharashtra, so far;
(b) the implementation framework adopted for mangrove expansion to strengthen coastal resilience, conserve biodiversity and support sustainable livelihoods of coastal communities;
(c) the monitoring and outcome indicators used to assess ecological and livelihood impacts under the scheme; and
(d) whether the Ministry proposes to scale up the MISHTI scheme to additional coastal areas with enhanced funding support and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made in the implementation of Mission Mausam, launched under IMD Vision 2047, with High Performance Computing (HPC) augmentation to 21 PetaFlops for high-resolution weather forecasting, AI/ML integration and seamless services;
(b) the improvements in forecast accuracy for cyclones, monsoons and heatwaves and economic impact quantified; 
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed public benefit and proposes Phase II expansion; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the implementation status of Prime Minister’s Development Initiative for North East (PM-DevINE) scheme, State-wise;
(b) the infrastructure projects completed in connectivity, power, water and social sectors, State-wise;
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed the extent to which development gaps have been addressed under the scheme;
(d) if so, the details thereof, State-wise;
(e) whether Government proposes to extend the scheme beyond its current period; and
(f) if so, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) the major initiatives undertaken by the Department of Posts to strengthen its presence in parcel and e-commerce logistics, including technological upgrades, logistics modernisation and tie-ups with domestic and global e-commerce platforms;
(b) the growth recorded in parcel traffic and logistics services during the last three years and measures adopted to enhance market competitiveness and service reliability;
(c) whether the Department has assessed the impact of these initiatives on revenue generation and operational efficiency; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, including financial performance indicators and future expansion strategy?

(a) the progress made under the Samagra Shiksha Scheme, including details of infrastructure development, teacher capacity building and quality enhancement measures undertaken to align with the National Education Policy, 2020;
(b) the number of schools upgraded, new residential schools/hostels established, additional classrooms constructed and ICT-enabled smart schools developed during this period, State-wise;
(c) whether the Ministry proposes to introduce additional performance-linked incentives or special support mechanisms for States demonstrating exemplary outcomes under Samagra Shiksha; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has completed the computerisation of the offices of the Registrar Cooperative Society (RCS) in all States and UTs;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including funds allocated, released and utilised as of January, 2026, State-wise/UT-wise;
(c) whether any State/UT has reported delays or implementation challenges in the computerisation initiative;
(d) if so, the reasons therefor, including the corrective measures taken by the Ministry;
(e) whether the computerisation initiative has resulted in measurable improvements in the functioning of RCS offices; and
(f) if so, details thereof, including reduction in time taken for registration, approval and regulatory compliance of cooperative societies?

(a) whether the Ministry has evaluated how increased financial assistance and technology deployment strengthened Urban Flood Risk Management Programme (UFRMP);
(b) whether the Ministry has put in place mechanisms for timely implementation, real-time monitoring and accountability of projects sanctioned under UFRMP;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether any evaluation has been undertaken to measure tangible flood-resilience outcomes, including reduction in urban flood incidence, response time, damage to infrastructure and loss of life and property; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?
