(a) the increase in fish production by December, 2025 after the launch of the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY);
(b) the number of women who are expected to benefit from the distribution of funds under the scheme by December, 2025 in the country, including Jharkhand;
(c) whether support has been provided for cold chain, processing and packaging under the scheme until December, 2025; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the key developments undertaken to expand and operationalise the PM SHRI(PM Schools for Rising India) schools scheme in alignment with the objectives of the National Education Policy, 2020;
(b) the details of additional schools approved or funded recently and the criteria adopted for their selection across States and Union Territories; and
(c) the measures taken to strengthen infrastructure, teacher training and digital learning facilities in PM SHRI schools to enable them to function as exemplar institutions, State-wise, and particularly in Gujarat?

(a) the key projects operationalised under Namami Gange Mission Phase-II during 2025, including major sewage treatment plants commissioned;
(b) the total sewage treatment capacity created under the Mission and its impact on Ganga water quality improvement;
(c) the biodiversity conservation achievements, including the status of Gangetic dolphin population and afforestation along the river; and
(d) the roadmap for achieving the Mission's objectives of Nirmal and Aviral Dhara by 2026?

(a) the current status of functional household tap connections under the Jal Jeevan Mission along with the number and percentage of rural households covered;
(b) the States and Union Territories which have achieved 100 per cent 'Har Ghar Jal' (tap water in every home) status and the timelines for achieving universal coverage in the remaining States; 
(c) the extent to which schools and Anganwadi Centres across the country have been covered with tap connections; and
(d) the coverage of tap water connections in school and Anganwadi Centres across the country especially in the States of Maharastra and Uttar Pardesh?

(a) the total number of houses sanctioned, grounded and the ones for which Bhoomi Pujan has been performed since the inception of Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban 2.0, along with the progress made, State-wise;
(b) the details of the Angikaar 2025 campaign conducted from September to October 2025 and its results in accelerating the implementation of the final phase;
(c) the measures being taken to include women beneficiaries and persons with disabilities under the scheme; and
(d) the financial provisions allocated to the States and the Central assistance released under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Urban 2.0?

(a) the category-wise details of total quantity of coal offered and actually allocated in 2025 under various components of the Scheme for Harnessing and Allocating Koyala Transparently in India (SHAKTI) Policy;
(b) the extent to which coal linkages granted under SHAKTI Policy have been utilized for power generation capacity;
(c) the criteria and timelines prescribed for allocation of coal linkages under the revised SHAKTI Policy; and
(d) the measures that have been taken to ensure better utilization of coal proposed through linkage auctions and optimal use of domestic coal resources?

(a) the details of the Navi Mumbai International airport inaugurated in October 2025, including its capacity, key features and expected impact on regional aviation connectivity;
(b) the number of greenfield airports currently under development across the country and their expected timelines for operationalisation;
(c) the steps being taken to ensure sustainable aviation practices at newly developed airports, including solar capacity integration and Sustainable Aviation Fuel infrastructure; and
(d) the employment generation and economic benefits anticipated from these airport projects?

(a) the number of Rural Self-Employment Training Institutes (RSETIs) currently operational in the country;
(b) whether Government has achieved the objective for which RSETIs were launched;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) the total number of youth trained and settled (self-employment or wage employment) during the last five years and the current year;
(e) whether any recent evaluation or review has been undertaken to identify challenges related to training quality, credit linkage, or post-training handholding;
(f) if so, the major findings and corrective measures initiated; and
(g) the details of major revisions introduced under RSETI 2.0 compared to RSETI 1.0?

(a) the current status of implementation of the PM e-Bus Sewa–Payment Security Mechanism (PSM) Scheme, including the number of electric buses deployed or operationalised so far under the Scheme;
(b) the total number of payment security support claims processed to date, the quantum of funds released from PSM;
(c) whether any instances of Public Transport Authorities (PTAs) payment defaults have been recorded;
(d) if so, the corrective measures undertaken thereof;
(e) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of the operational performance, utilisation rates or service outcomes of electric buses supported under the Scheme; and
(f) if so, the key findings?

(a) the key measures taken by Government to enhance the affordability of healthcare;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any initiatives to strengthen India’s position as a global destination for medical value tourism and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the steps being taken to improve collaboration with the healthcare industry and private sector to promote inclusive and high-quality medical infrastructure; and
(d) the measures proposed to promote traditional systems of medicine and wellness as part of India’s broader healthcare and export strategy?

(a) the GST rate rationalisation for drones and flight/motion simulators announced in September 2025, the manner in which these changes promote Ease of Doing Business in aviation and emerging technologies;
(b) the number of pilot training organisations and aviation-skilling centres that have benefited from these measures since the announcement;
(c) Government’s assessment of the manner in which GST exemptions will boost employment, manufacturing (Make in India) and regional aviation training hubs; and
(d) the steps being taken to monitor and ensure effectiveness of these reforms in expanding drone ecosystem and training infrastructure nationwide?

(a) whether the Ministry has plans to collaborate with educational institutions to create certified training programs for managing and maintaining the next generation of advanced cold chain infrastructure;
(b) the manner in which the Ministry is ensuring that Agro Processing Clusters (APCs) are located near high-value crop production zones to reduce post-harvest losses and improve farmers income; and
(c) whether the Ministry has introduced third-party auditing to monitor the use of APC infrastructure such as primary processing and collection centers and ensure the benefits reach farmers?

